# Face Recognition Attendance Portal — Full Production Upgrade

## Overview

You already have a solid foundation in `Facial-Attendance-System--main` — a FastAPI backend with DeepFace/YOLOv8, a React/Vite frontend with role-based routing, dark/light theme, live webcam attendance, and SQLite. This plan **upgrades and extends** that codebase (rather than starting from scratch) into the full production-grade system you described.

The target is the `/Users/shreya/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-ManipalUniversityJaipur/Facial-Attendance-System--main` directory.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Migration: SQLite → PostgreSQL**
> The current system uses SQLite (`facial_attendance.db`). The plan migrates to PostgreSQL via Docker. All data in the existing SQLite file will need to be re-seeded. Should we keep SQLite as a fallback for local dev?

> [!WARNING]
> **Face Model Change**
> Current: YOLOv8n (general object detection) + DeepFace Facenet512
> Plan: SSD MobileNet v1 (via `@vladmandic/face-api` in browser) + DeepFace Facenet512 (server-side)
> The browser-side face-api.js models (~6MB) must be downloaded and served from `/public/models/`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Color Scheme Remap**
> Current palette: indigo/violet dark (`#6366f1`, `#0f111a`).
> Spec calls for: Navy blue `#1e3a5f` primary + white + orange `#f97316` accent.
> All CSS variables and UI will be updated to match the university ERP style.

---

